          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.083,
            0.826,
            0.103
          ],
          "content": "9. Match the entries in Column I with those in Column II."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.107,
            0.88,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "| Column I | Column II |\n| --- | --- |\n| (i) Concave mirror | (a) Spherical mirror with a reflecting surface that curves inwards. |\n| (ii) Convex mirror | (b) It forms an image which is always erect and diminished in size. |\n| (iii) Convex lens | (c) Object placed behind it may appear inverted at some distance. |\n| (iv) Concave lens | (d) Object placed behind it always appears diminished in size. |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_table_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.31,
            0.882,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": "10. The following question is based on Assertion/Reason. **Assertion:** Convex mirrors are preferred for observing the traffic behind us."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.374,
            0.882,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "**Reason:** Convex mirrors provide a significantly larger view area than plane mirrors."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.417,
            0.557,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "Choose the correct option:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.44,
            0.882,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "(i) Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.481,
            0.882,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation for Assertion."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.521,
            0.762,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.544,
            0.738,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.571,
            0.882,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "11. In Fig. 10.27, note that O stands for object, M for mirror, and I for image. Which of the following statements is true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.634,
            0.882,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": "(i) Figure (a) indicates a plane mirror and Figure (b) indicates a concave mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.674,
            0.882,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Figure (a) indicates a convex mirror and Figure (b) indicates a concave mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.715,
            0.882,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "indicates a convex mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.744,
            0.2,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 10.27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.756,
            0.882,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Figure (a) indicates a plane mirror and Figure (b) indicates a convex mirror."
